        "original_id": "03551633-e955-52b0-810f-e0dc66217fc0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikhail Lomonosov\n- Products: Akademik Lomonosov\n- Organizations: Bilibino Nuclear Power Plant\n- Concepts: Russian polymathy, scientific discoveries\n\nFacts:\n- Mikhail Vasilyevich Lomonosov was a Russian polymath, scientist, and writer who lived from 1711 to 1765 and made important contributions to literature, education, and science.\n- Mikhail Lomonosov worked in natural science, chemistry, physics, mineralogy, history, art, philology, and optical devices.\n- Mikhail Lomonosov is credited with discoveries including the atmosphere of Venus and the law of mass conservation in chemical reactions.\n- The ship Akademik Lomonosov was named after Academician Mikhail Lomonosov.\n- Plans were announced for Bilibino Nuclear Power Plant to begin shutdown procedures in 2019 and to be replaced by the floating nuclear power station Akademik Lomonosov.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "813ec54a-b481-57bc-a70c-d3f38e58f341",
        "text": "Page: Akademik Lomonosov. Sentence: The ship was named after Academician Mikhail Lomonosov.\nPage: Mikhail Lomonosov. Sentence: Mikhail Vasilyevich Lomonosov ( ; Russian: Михаи́л (Михáйло) Васи́льевич Ломоно́сов ; ] ; November 19 [O.S. November 8] 1711 – April 15 [O.S. April 4] 1765 ) was a Russian polymath, scientist and writer, who made important contributions to literature, education, and science.\nPage: Mikhail Lomonosov. Sentence: Among his discoveries were the atmosphere of Venus and the Law of Mass Conservation in chemical reactions. His spheres of science were natural science, chemistry, physics, mineralogy, history, art, philology, optical devices and others.\nPage: Bilibino Nuclear Power Plant. Sentence: Plans to begin a shutdown procedure of the plant in 2019 have been announced, and it will be replaced by the floating nuclear power station \"Akademik Lomonosov\".",
